use flock/algebra/whole/hath_eke.tung
use ilk/two.tung

## negation, and `b -+ a`, which negateth `b` and addeth `a`: `a` less `b`.
## each type supplieth `-+` directly, so integers and floats subtract in one
## native step; `group_+` and `ring` prove it agreeth with negation and `+`.
show flock hath_-: [α: *, *] {
  let -: [α, α]
  let -+: [α, α, α]
}

## `+` on `𝟚` is exclusive or, so each value is its own negation.
bizen: 𝟚 hath_- {
  let -: [a:] ≔ a
  let -+: [b:, a:] ≔ b + a
}
